note: gradlew invoked as gradlew.bat (Windows runner).
note: the Gradle module is :android (settings.gradle.kts maps projectDir=app); the prompt gate's :app:
      placeholder is this repo's :android: module - same adaptation the sibling 0164 VehicleSelect / 0157
      RangePicker gates record.
note: surface ships as flat files under com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/ (the prompt's allowed-files VehiclePicker.*
      path); the mandated directory cannot form a valid Kotlin package (hyphen + PascalCase leaf), so the
      package is io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.vehiclepicker with @file:Suppress(InvalidPackageDeclaration)
      - identical to the VehicleSelect / RangePicker precedent. Tests live in the matching real package path
      under test/ and androidTest/.
note: the gate's extensionless -Path .../shared-surfaces/VehiclePicker matches no file, so the placeholder
      scan below targets the real .kt files for genuine coverage (VehicleSelect precedent).
note: P1/S8 wiring - usePinned had no Android binding; the shared-core PinnedStore (P1/S8) existed but was
      unwired and api/cache are not reachable from composition, so DataContainer (the doc-stated 'single seam
      prompts widen - register their store') exposes a new pinnedStore = PinnedStore(HttpPinnedRepository(...))
      mirroring vehiclesStore. VehiclePicker binds selection+fleet+pins; no HTTP in the view.
note: i18n reuses existing P1/S10 catalog keys (vehiclePicker.aria/statusBar.vehicle.fallback/common.*/
      mqtt.stale/freshness.updating); apps/android strings.xml is GENERATED from apps/shared/i18n - editing it
      would drift + is out of allowed-files scope.

